{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"and the people wept that night\"</b> — for in the evening the spies came to their tents, as they went out from before Moses, and in the morning they rose early and all of them murmured against Moses and Aaron. And thus Moses said: \"and you murmured in your tents\" (Deuteronomy 1:27), for it was in their tents that they spoke the words of a murmur. And our Sages said (Ta'anit 29a): they wept a weeping without cause, and I have fixed for them a weeping for all generations. Now I do not know from what allusion in the passage they derived this, but it is a full verse (Psalms 106:24–27): \"And they despised the desirable land, and did not believe His word. And they murmured in their tents, they did not hearken to the voice of YHWH. And He lifted up His hand against them, to make them fall in the wilderness, and to cast down their seed among the nations, and to scatter them among the lands.\" Perhaps this may be expounded from the verse (v. 31): \"and your little ones, of whom you said would become a prey\" — one may say: and your little ones, as you said would become a prey, so they shall be when the time of their visitation comes, for I punish the iniquity of fathers upon children, and I will bring them now to know the land in knowledge alone, but not that they shall inherit it for generations. And Scripture hints at something like this, and does not intend to decree evil, but only in the manner of reproof upon the condition."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:06.889197452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}